  "domain": "governance",
  "definition": "The Paris Agreement is a legally binding international treaty on climate change, adopted under the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change (UNFCCC) at COP21 in December 2015 and entering into force in November 2016. It establishes a long-term global temperature goal, requiring parties to limit the increase in global average temperature to well below 2 degrees Celsius above pre-industrial levels while pursuing efforts to limit warming to 1.5 degrees Celsius. Each signatory submits Nationally Determined Contributions (NDCs) \u2014 self-defined emissions-reduction pledges \u2014 subject to a five-year review and ratchet mechanism designed to progressively strengthen ambition. The treaty also creates a transparency framework for monitoring, reporting, and verification, and provisions for climate finance, technology transfer, and capacity building to support developing nations.",
